IMPORT prelude

-- Limited Partnerships Act 2008 (Singapore) -- constitution and liability (s 3), default rules (s 5), the management bar and its
-- safe harbours (s 6 and the First Schedule), distributions and clawback (s 7), dissolution (s 8), the effect of registration
-- (s 10), the name (s 16), local managers (s 28) and bankrupts (s 29).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LPA2008.txt (amendments to
-- Act 21 of 2024, in force 9 December 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 18 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. Near-whole: the rules of law (Part 2)
-- and the parts of registration (Part 3) that change a partner's liability. Not encoded: the Registrar's procedures, name
-- reservation and restrictions (ss 17 to 17B), changes in particulars, records, inspection, and the general offences.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limited Partnerships Act 2008 -- partners`

§§ `3, 10 -- liability`

-- s 3(2): a limited partnership must have "one or more general partners; and ... one or more limited partners". (3): a general
-- partner is liable for all debts incurred while a general partner. (4): a limited partner is not liable beyond the agreed
-- contribution, "solely by reason of" being a limited partner -- subject to ss 6(2) and 10.
-- s 10(1): "A limited partner of a firm is DEEMED TO BE A GENERAL PARTNER of the firm unless the limited partner is REGISTERED
-- as a limited partner." (2): likewise the firm is a general partnership until a limited partner is registered.
-- (3), (4): someone who dealt with the firm before registration may treat it, and a former general partner, as general until
-- they have notice; (5), (6): registration is notice only to those who had NO dealings before it.
DECLARE Partner HAS
    `agreed to be a limited partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a limited partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took part in management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the debt arose while taking part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the creditor dealt with the firm before registration without notice` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the partner` IS A Partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is liable without limit for the debt` IF
        (NOT `the partner`'s `agreed to be a limited partner`)
    OR  (NOT `the partner`'s `registered as a limited partner`)
    OR  `the partner`'s `the creditor dealt with the firm before registration without notice`
    OR  (`the partner`'s `took part in management` AND `the partner`'s `the debt arose while taking part`)

GIVEN `general partners` IS A NUMBER, `limited partners` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the firm can be a limited partnership` IF
    `general partners` AT LEAST 1 AND `limited partners` AT LEAST 1

§§ `6 and First Schedule -- the management bar`

-- s 6(1): a limited partner "must not take part in the management" and cannot bind the firm. (2): one who does is liable "for all
-- debts and obligations ... incurred WHILE SO TAKING PART in the management as though the limited partner were a general
-- partner" -- not for debts before or after.
-- (3), First Schedule: these do NOT count as taking part in management (the list is not exhaustive -- (4)): contracting with
-- the firm; acting as its employee or agent; being a director or shareholder of a corporate general partner; advising;
-- reviewing accounts; acting as GUARANTOR; enforcing rights; attending meetings; voting on amendments, on any transaction
-- (including investments and the removal of a general partner); suing when the general partners without good cause refuse;
-- winding up under PA 1890 s 39; and "having all or any part of one's name included in the name of the limited partnership".
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `negotiating contracts with suppliers for the firm`
    `signing cheques for the firm`
    `voting to remove a general partner`
    `guaranteeing the firm's bank loan`
    `advising the general partner on strategy`
    `being a director of the corporate general partner`
    `having their name in the firm's name`
    `suing after the general partners refused without good cause`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a safe harbour` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `negotiating contracts with suppliers for the firm` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `signing cheques for the firm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5, 7 -- default rules and distributions`

-- s 5, subject to agreement: (a) ordinary matters are decided by a majority of the GENERAL partners; (b) a person may become a
-- partner "without the consent of the existing limited partners".
-- s 7(2): a limited partner must refund a distribution only if ALL of: (a) every general partner was insolvent at the time or
-- became so as a result; (b) the limited partner knew or ought to have known; and (c) every general partner is made bankrupt or
-- wound up within ONE YEAR after the distribution.
DECLARE Distribution HAS
    `every general partner was or became insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the limited partner knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every general partner was made bankrupt or wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months until the last bankruptcy or winding up` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the distribution` IS A Distribution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the limited partner must refund the distribution` IF
        `the distribution`'s `every general partner was or became insolvent`
    AND `the distribution`'s `the limited partner knew or ought to have known`
    AND `the distribution`'s `every general partner was made bankrupt or wound up`
    AND `the distribution`'s `months until the last bankruptcy or winding up` AT MOST 12

§§ `8 -- dissolution`

-- s 8, subject to agreement: (1) a limited partner "is not entitled to dissolve the partnership by notice"; (2) the firm is NOT
-- dissolved by the death, dissolution, bankruptcy or liquidation of a limited partner; (3) a charge on a limited partner's
-- share is not a ground for the others to dissolve; (5) mental incapacity of a limited partner is a ground only if their share
-- cannot otherwise be realised. (6): the general partners wind up, unless the court orders otherwise.
-- (Under the Partnership Act 1890 ss 32, 33, each of these WOULD dissolve an ordinary partnership.)
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `a limited partner gives notice to dissolve`
    `a limited partner dies`
    `a limited partner becomes bankrupt`
    `a general partner dies`
    `a general partner gives notice to dissolve`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event, `the agreement provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event dissolves the partnership` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `a general partner dies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a general partner gives notice to dissolve` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the agreement provides otherwise`

§§ `16, 28, 29 -- name, local manager, bankrupts`

-- s 16(1): the name must contain "limited partnership" or "LP"; $5,000 fine on each general partner.
-- s 28(1): if EVERY general partner is ordinarily resident outside Singapore, the Registrar may require a local manager, who
-- (2) bears a general partner's liabilities for the filing obligations.
-- s 29(1): an undischarged bankrupt may not take part in management without the High Court's or the Official Assignee's
-- permission -- $10,000 or 2 years.
GIVEN `the name contains "limited partnership" or "LP"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name complies` IF `the name contains "limited partnership" or "LP"`

GIVEN `general partners resident outside Singapore` IS A NUMBER, `general partners` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may require a local manager` IF
    `general partners resident outside Singapore` EQUALS `general partners` AND `general partners` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `has court or Official Assignee permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `managing the firm is an offence` IF
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` AND (NOT `has court or Official Assignee permission`)
